  <shortname>SSEZL</shortname>
  <fullname>Supporting Social and Emotional Well-being in Young Children - Zephirina Lansiquot</fullname>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <summary>&lt;p class="MsoNormal"&gt;The purpose of this module on Social and Emotional Well-Being in Young Children is to provide Early Childhood Education teachers with practical, job-embedded professional opportunities to learn about the importance of 3 to 4-year-old children’s development of social and emotional skills for present well-being, plus future school and lifelong success. Participants will learn evidence-based practices to enhance children’s social and emotional development.&lt;span style="mso-spacerun: yes;"&gt;  &lt;/span&gt;The Module is comprised of four interactive, synchronous sessions, two associated asynchronous learning activities, and two products that are designed to assist participants with their daily practice. These practical, job-embedded activities and products will enable participants to apply the new knowledge and skills that they are learning in the Module in their work contexts.&lt;span style="mso-spacerun: yes;"&gt;  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</summary>
